---
name: relative-cd
enabled: true
event: bash
action: warn
conditions:
  - field: command
    operator: regex_match
    pattern: (^|&&|;|\|\|)\s*cd\s+(?!["']?(/|\$|~|-\s*$))
---

ATTENTION: relative `cd`. In many sessions the cwd RESETS between Bash calls ("Shell cwd was reset to ...") — `cd apps/web` in one call does not carry over to the next, and has already caused "cd: apps/web: No such file or directory".

Use an ABSOLUTE path — `cd {{ project_root }}/apps/web && ...` — or better, embed the absolute path directly in the command (e.g. `bash {{ project_root }}/apps/web/scripts/ui-evidence.sh`) without depending on the cwd.
